  "description": "Audubon, Paiute, Toll, and kinda Pawnee. Way chossier than I expected which made this slow going, which had major repercussions. Should have picked something less climby and more runny. Got rained and hailed on about a mile from the end. Really good scrambling class 3-5 to be had here if you choose the spicy lines (Toll is the marquis climbing here). Had just done 5.7k feet of biking to get the the trailhead, so that made this a 10k foot adventure!",
